
══════ Cenário 01 — Registo, KYC, conta no shard certo e login ══════
(2026-11-23T22:06:25Z)

▶ 1. Registo de um cliente da Europa e de um cliente da América
  POST /auth/register -> HTTP 201
  ✔ cliente EU registado (HTTP 201)
    {
      "id": "0718af52-4b4c-4727-b8ed-720730873966",
      "status": "PENDENTE_VERIFICACAO",
      "region": "EU"
    }
  POST /auth/register -> HTTP 201
  ✔ cliente AM registado (HTTP 201)
    {
      "id": "3e048cdc-a941-4fa6-9558-3ff40e7476a6",
      "status": "PENDENTE_VERIFICACAO",
      "region": "AM"
    }

▶ 2. Ainda pendente: o login é recusado
  POST /auth/login -> HTTP 403
  ✔ login recusado enquanto PENDENTE_VERIFICACAO (HTTP 403)
    "conta não ativa (estado: PENDENTE_VERIFICACAO)"

▶ 3. Na BD, o documento de identificação está cifrado (AES-256-GCM)
  $ psql "host=pg-core.global.local dbname=auth" -c "SELECT email, status, encode(substr(document_id_enc,1,24),'hex') AS document_id_enc FROM users WHERE id = '0718af52-4b4c-4727-b8ed-720730873966'"
               email            |        status        |                 document_id_enc                  
    ----------------------------+----------------------+--------------------------------------------------
     maria.1795471585@demo.test | PENDENTE_VERIFICACAO | a6bdb0682da934ef747fb41e244c68b2ceb7a92fae02424f
    (1 row)
    

▶ 4. O operador aprova o KYC dos dois clientes
  POST /auth/login -> HTTP 200
  GET /admin/users?status=PENDENTE_VERIFICACAO -> HTTP 200
  pendentes: teste.2fb2bae7@cliente.test, teste.7fd6dbb7@cliente.test, teste.388d05eb@cliente.test, teste.bc076af7@cliente.test, teste.81adb32c@cliente.test, teste.7f6c1b00@cliente.test, maria.1795471585@demo.test, john.1795471585@demo.test
  POST /admin/users/0718af52-4b4c-4727-b8ed-720730873966/approve-kyc -> HTTP 200
  ✔ KYC EU aprovado (HTTP 200)
    {
      "iban": "GS-EU-00000008",
      "user_id": "0718af52-4b4c-4727-b8ed-720730873966",
      "region": "EU",
      "currency": "EUR",
      "balance": "0.00",
      "status": "ATIVA",
      "daily_limit": "50000.00",
      "created_at": "2026-11-23T22:06:26.675249+00:00",
      "closed_at": null,
      "region_unavailable": false,
      "created": true
    }
  POST /admin/users/3e048cdc-a941-4fa6-9558-3ff40e7476a6/approve-kyc -> HTTP 200
  ✔ KYC AM aprovado (HTTP 200)
    {
      "iban": "GS-AM-00000039",
      "user_id": "3e048cdc-a941-4fa6-9558-3ff40e7476a6",
      "region": "AM",
      "currency": "USD",
      "balance": "0.00",
      "status": "ATIVA",
      "daily_limit": "50000.00",
      "created_at": "2026-11-23T22:06:26.762639+00:00",
      "closed_at": null,
      "region_unavailable": false,
      "created": true
    }

▶ 5. Consulta direta a cada shard: cada conta só existe no nó da sua região
  pg-europa:
  $ psql "host=pg-europa.global.local,pg-europa-replica.global.local target_session_attrs=read-write dbname=bank" -c "SELECT iban, currency, balance FROM accounts WHERE user_id IN ('0718af52-4b4c-4727-b8ed-720730873966','3e048cdc-a941-4fa6-9558-3ff40e7476a6')"
          iban      | currency | balance 
    ----------------+----------+---------
     GS-EU-00000008 | EUR      |    0.00
    (1 row)
    
  pg-america:
  $ psql "host=pg-america.global.local,pg-america-replica.global.local target_session_attrs=read-write dbname=bank" -c "SELECT iban, currency, balance FROM accounts WHERE user_id IN ('0718af52-4b4c-4727-b8ed-720730873966','3e048cdc-a941-4fa6-9558-3ff40e7476a6')"
          iban      | currency | balance 
    ----------------+----------+---------
     GS-AM-00000039 | USD      |    0.00
    (1 row)
    
  ✔ GS-EU-00000008 só no pg-europa, GS-AM-00000039 só no pg-america
  a réplica também a tem (replicação streaming):
  $ psql "host=pg-europa-replica.global.local dbname=bank" -c "SELECT iban, pg_is_in_recovery() AS replica FROM accounts WHERE iban = 'GS-EU-00000008'"
          iban      | replica 
    ----------------+---------
     GS-EU-00000008 | t
    (1 row)
    

